V - In view of the above, I recommend to this High Command to organize a "UFO Registry" of a confidential nature, in which all phenomena observed in the Brazilian airspace, with all available data, including those obtained through subsequent official investigations, should be chronologically recorded.

Parallelly, an Assessment Commission will assign a reliability rating to each registry.

Any stray observations or records within this High Command should be submitted to the Assessment Commission for proper classification and archiving.

VI - Access to the archived data should allow for various "searches", such as:

1. Reliability rating;
2. Date;
3. Location;
4. Particular aspects of the registry.

VII - The official establishment of the aforementioned service, as well as the appointment of the officers responsible for its operation, should be the subject of a Confidential Order from the Minister of Aeronautics.

VIII - Lastly, I recommend that the officers to be part of the Assessment Commission should be free from any preconceived personal ideas or opinions. The freedom from bias is essential.

